# License for "L'ultima alba di Dalmasca"

"L'ultima alba di Dalmasca" ("The Last Dawn of Dalmasca") is a fan novel, with an audiobook, based on *Final Fantasy XII*. It is a work of fiction, free of charge, free to share and made on a non-profit basis.

Copyright © 2026 maxeo

## Summary

You may read, listen to, copy, share, translate and adapt the novel and the audiobook, as long as you credit the source, do not make money from them and release your versions under the same license.

This summary does not replace the licenses listed below.

## Which license applies

| Material | License |
|---|---|
| Novel, chapters, working materials and pronunciation dictionary | CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 |
| Audiobook | CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, plus the voice model terms |
| Code: scripts, `Dockerfile`, web player and service worker | MIT |

The player is in `docs/`. Its code consists of `index.html`, `sw.js` and `manifest.webmanifest`. Audio and synchronized text in `docs/` follow the rules for the audiobook and the novel.

### Novel and audiobook: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

The original contributions of this project are released under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International license.

- Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode
- Summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

The license requires you to:

- **Give credit:** state the title, the author and a link to the project, indicate any changes and include a link to the license. Do not suggest that the author endorses your version.
- **Stay non-commercial:** do not sell the work or use it to obtain a commercial advantage or payment.
- **Share alike:** if you adapt the work, release the result under the same license or a compatible one.

You can credit the source like this:

> "L'ultima alba di Dalmasca" by maxeo, https://github.com/maxeo/ultima-alba-di-dalmasca, licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

### Audiobook: voice model

The audio is generated with Coqui's XTTS v2 model, distributed under the Coqui Public Model License 1.0.0, which allows only non-commercial use of the model and its output. Anyone who receives a copy of the audio also receives this reference to the terms: https://coqui.ai/cpml.txt

The voice is synthetic and does not belong to a real person identified by this project.

### Code: MIT

The code may be reused under the MIT License, whose full text is at the end of this file.

## What this license does not cover

*Final Fantasy XII* and the world of Ivalice, including their story, characters, places, names and trademarks, belong to Square Enix and their respective owners.

This project is an unofficial fan work. It is not endorsed by or affiliated with Square Enix, and Square Enix has not granted it any permission. The license applies only to the rights that the author of this project can grant, and it gives no rights in any element owned by Square Enix. Anyone who reuses the work must assess for themselves whether those rights are needed.

The same applies to third-party software used to generate the audio, such as ebook2audiobook, which has its own license.

## Other information

- **Work of fiction:** the characters and events are imaginary. Any reference to real people or real events is coincidental.
- **Artificial intelligence:** the text was written with artificial intelligence models under the author's direction, and the audio is generated by a voice model. The license applies only to the extent that rights exist in these materials.
- **No warranty:** the work is provided as is, to the extent permitted by law.
- **Reports:** rights holders can request a correction or removal by opening an issue at https://github.com/maxeo/ultima-alba-di-dalmasca/issues

This information explains the project and does not change the terms of the licenses listed above.

